Metadata-Version: 2.1
Name: colorpy
Version: 0.1.2
Summary: Color calculations with physical descriptions of light spectra
Home-page: http://markkness.net/colorpy/
Author: Mark Kness
Author-email: mkness@alumni.utexas.net
License: GNU Lesser GPL Version 3
Description:
        ColorPy is a Python package to convert physical descriptions of light -
        spectra of light intensity vs. wavelength - into RGB colors that can
        be drawn on a computer screen.
        It provides a nice set of attractive plots that you can make of such
        spectra, and some other color related functions as well.

        ColorPy targets Python 3.8 or newer and is tested on modern interpreters.
        This release ensures intra-package imports resolve correctly when the
        library is installed via pip.

